{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3381300/extras/fb013dad70cfa2ed8628ed8193b89a0a.poster.avif?t=1770496010\" width=720 height=404 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3381300/extras/fb013dad70cfa2ed8628ed8193b89a0a.webm?t=1770496010\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3381300/extras/fb013dad70cfa2ed8628ed8193b89a0a.mp4?t=1770496010\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Steam &amp; Iron: Battle of Port Arthur</strong> is a real-time naval simulator set in the era of early 20th-century steamships. Step into the shoes of Japanese Admiral Heihachiro Togo aboard his flagship battleship <i>Mikasa</i> and lead your fleet into battle against the Russian navy\u2019s formidable squadrons of battleships, cruisers, and torpedo boats.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Our game faithfully simulates naval engagements between individual ships and fleets in the Yellow Sea during the Japanese Navy\u2019s siege of the Russian naval base at Port Arthur.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Play through ready-made missions or create your own using a built-in editor.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game features ships from the Russian First Pacific Squadron and the Japanese Navy (Nippon Kaigun).</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tactical naval combat is carefully simulated, factoring in ship positioning, speed, sea conditions, fire and flood control systems, and accuracy adjustments.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Weather conditions, sea states, and time of day directly affect combat dynamics.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >All ships are based on real historical prototypes with accurate technical specifications.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game includes dozens of military and civilian ships from both fleets, with more being added over time.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3381300/extras/5e38ed83f5eb0c292ca85e51e664ff5e.poster.avif?t=1770496010\" width=720 height=404 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3381300/extras/5e38ed83f5eb0c292ca85e51e664ff5e.webm?t=1770496010\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3381300/extras/5e38ed83f5eb0c292ca85e51e664ff5e.mp4?t=1770496010\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Planned Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Dynamic campaign for the battles in the Yellow Sea for both sides.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Save and load functionality during missions.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Naval operations in other theaters (e.g., Vladivostok, Tsushima).</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >New ships.</p></li></ul>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3381300?t=1770496010","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/3381300?t=1770496010","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3381300/0882be3eded12c2efb910be867072d3d8a4390b3/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1770496010","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3381300/0882be3eded12c2efb910be867072d3d8a4390b3/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1770496010","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3381300/extras/fb013dad70cfa2ed8628ed8193b89a0a.poster.avif?t=1770496010\" width=720 height=404 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3381300/extras/fb013dad70cfa2ed8628ed8193b89a0a.webm?t=1770496010\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3381300/extras/fb013dad70cfa2ed8628ed8193b89a0a.mp4?t=1770496010\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Steam &amp; Iron: Battle of Port Arthur</strong> is a real-time naval simulator set in the era of early 20th-century steamships. Step into the shoes of Japanese Admiral Heihachiro Togo aboard his flagship battleship <i>Mikasa</i> and lead your fleet into battle against the Russian navy\u2019s formidable squadrons of battleships, cruisers, and torpedo boats.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Our game faithfully simulates naval engagements between individual ships and fleets in the Yellow Sea during the Japanese Navy\u2019s siege of the Russian naval base at Port Arthur.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Play through ready-made missions or create your own using a built-in editor.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game features ships from the Russian First Pacific Squadron and the Japanese Navy (Nippon Kaigun).</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Tactical naval combat is carefully simulated, factoring in ship positioning, speed, sea conditions, fire and flood control systems, and accuracy adjustments.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Weather conditions, sea states, and time of day directly affect combat dynamics.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >All ships are based on real historical prototypes with accurate technical specifications.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game includes dozens of military and civilian ships from both fleets, with more being added over time.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3381300/extras/5e38ed83f5eb0c292ca85e51e664ff5e.poster.avif?t=1770496010\" width=720 height=404 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3381300/extras/5e38ed83f5eb0c292ca85e51e664ff5e.webm?t=1770496010\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3381300/extras/5e38ed83f5eb0c292ca85e51e664ff5e.mp4?t=1770496010\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Planned Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Dynamic campaign for the battles in the Yellow Sea for both sides.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Save and load functionality during missions.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Naval operations in other theaters (e.g., Vladivostok, Tsushima).</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >New ships.</p></li></ul>","developers":["Goydalka Games"],"genres":[{"description":"Indie","id":"23"},{"description":"Simulation","id":"28"},{"description":"Strategy","id":"2"},{"description":"Early Access","id":"70"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3381300/header.jpg?t=1770496010","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>"},"mac_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>"},"movies":[{"dash_av1":"https://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/3381300/801494/4fb65d1a31d933557428b3fec2e5db4ab2b4d35f/17508457